      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">In the classroom</p>
        <h3>Courses at Georgia Tech</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>BIOS 2300, Introduction to Ecology.</strong> A large lecture
          course, covering all of the major topics in ecology (featuring lots of lizards).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>BIOS 4460, Communicating Biological Research.</strong> A professional
          development workshop class for undergraduates, learning how to 
          communicate their research to scientific audiences.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">For younger readers</p>
        <h3>The Lizard Scientists</h3>
        <p>
          Lizards on the Loose features in <a href="https://www.harpercollins.com/products/the-lizard-scientists-dorothy-hinshaw-patent"><em>The Lizard Scientists: Studying
          Evolution in Action</em></a> (Clarion Books, 2022), written by Dorothy
          Hinshaw Patent with photographs by Nate Dappen and Neil Losin.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Ongoing</p>
        <h3>Events and workshops</h3>
        <p>
          The lab runs coordinated outreach each year: nocturnal biodiversity
          walks at Fairchild, introductions to R for high school students, career
          workshops, and teacher forums. 
        </p>
      </div>
